<title>BELGIUM: Belgian money market supply lowered in week.</title>
<headline>Belgian money market supply lowered in week.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian central bank said it withdrew liquidity from the money market in the week to April 7 to offset a fall in the amount of notes in circulation.</p>
<p>(figures from the weekly statement in bln francs) -</p>
<p> Foreign currency reserves	   450.52 (+ 0.06)</p>
<p> Advances against pledged security  13.16 (+ 4.47)</p>
<p> Commercial bills			  2.66 (+ 0.02)</p>
<p> Securities portfolio		   23.81 (  0.00)</p>
<p> Money market interventions*	 100.64 (- 6.94)</p>
<p> Bank notes in circulation	   459.99 (- 2.22)</p>
<p>* comprises repurchase agreements and interbank loans</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
